---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { formatDate } from "../lib/format";
import { formatFeeAmount } from "../lib/facts";
import { absoluteUrl, href } from "../lib/paths";

const guides = (await getCollection("guides")).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);
const featured = guides.filter((guide) => guide.data.featured);
const providers = await getCollection("providers");
const college = providers.find((item) => item.id === "collegeboxes");
const dorm = providers.find((item) => item.id === "dorm-room-movers");
const snapshot = [
  college?.data.fees.find((fee) => fee.id === "standard-box"),
  college?.data.fees.find((fee) => fee.id === "handling-tamu"),
  dorm?.data.fees.find((fee) => fee.id === "tier-box"),
  dorm?.data.fees.find((fee) => fee.id === "registration"),
].filter((fee) => fee != null);

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebSite",
  name: "Move-Out Desk",
  url: absoluteUrl("/"),
  description:
    "Independent comparison of Texas A&M summer storage: pickup services, local units, and shipping home.",
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: "Move-Out Desk",
    url: absoluteUrl("/"),
  },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Texas A&M summer storage, compared independently"
  description="Pickup services, College Station storage units, and shipping home, with every price linked to the page it came from. No ratings invented, no trackers."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">College Station, first campus</p>
      <h1>Summer storage for Texas A&M, with the receipts attached.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Move-Out Desk compares the ways to leave a College Station room: a company that picks the
        boxes up, a storage unit you rent yourself, or a shipment home. We print a number only when
        a public page states it, and we date the day we checked.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="notice">
      <p><strong>Checked {formatDate("2026-11-18")}.</strong></p>
      <p>
        Collegeboxes lists pickups on December 11, 2026 and May 10, 2027. Its school page also says
        full-service moving is currently unavailable. Both sentences are on the page.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        We are not Texas A&M. Collegeboxes says it has no active partnership with the university.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <h2>Start with the three guides that are written through</h2>
  <div class="card-grid three">
    {
      featured.map((guide) => (
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">{guide.data.eyebrow}</p>
          <h3>{guide.data.title}</h3>
          <p>{guide.data.description}</p>
          <a class="more" href={href(`/guides/${guide.id}`)}>
            Read the guide
          </a>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <h2>A few prices we could actually verify</h2>
  <p class="prose">
    These are starting points, not a quote. Open the source on the row. The
    <a href={href("/guides/texas-am-summer-storage")}>summer storage guide</a> has a calculator that uses
    the same figures.
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <caption>Verified starting prices for Texas A&M move-out</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Item</th>
          <th scope="col">Published amount</th>
          <th scope="col">Checked</th>
          <th scope="col">Source</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          snapshot.map((fee) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{fee.label}</th>
              <td>{formatFeeAmount(fee)}</td>
              <td>
                <time datetime={fee.lastVerified}>{formatDate(fee.lastVerified)}</time>
              </td>
              <td>
                <a href={fee.sourceUrl}>{fee.sourceLabel}</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What students are trying to solve</h2>
  <div class="card-grid two">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>Books and winter clothes for the summer</h3>
      <p>
        One long-running question in r/aggies is where to keep a lot of books and winter clothes
        over the summer, with climate control if the price is reasonable, instead of driving it all
        home. The climate comparison is the practical answer we can document.
      </p>
      <a href={href("/guides/college-station-climate-controlled")}>Climate-controlled units</a>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>A short gap, not a whole summer</h3>
      <p>
        Another thread asks for the cheapest month or so for a TV, a mini fridge, and a dresser
        between leases, in College Station or Bryan. Month-to-month units fit that better than a
        4-month pickup contract. The gap is the unpublished move-in fee.
      </p>
      <a href={href("/cities/college-station")}>College Station unit table</a>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted prose">
    Those threads are context for the questions, not reviews. We do not quote usernames or treat
    comments as prices.
    <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/aggies/comments/uil2rx/best_storage_units_in_cstat/">Summer storage thread</a>.
    <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/aggies/comments/6meysf/wheres_can_i_find_the_cheapest_shortterm_storage/">Short-term storage thread</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How a row gets on the site</h2>
  <ul class="clean prose">
    <li>A provider page, a facility page, or a university page states the fact.</li>
    <li>The row links that URL and shows the day we opened it.</li>
    <li>If two official pages disagree, the status says sources disagree.</li>
    <li>If the dollar amount is missing, the amount says not yet verified. We do not fill it in.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="prose">
    <a href={href("/schools/texas-am")}>Texas A&M guide</a> ·
    <a href={href("/compare")}>Head-to-head comparisons</a> ·
    <a href={href("/about")}>Who pays for this, which is nobody yet</a>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
